 Insights: Sales Trends & Customer Behaviour

- Sales show monthly variation indicating seasonal demand
- Majority of revenue comes from top countries (UK dominates)
- Few products contribute to most revenue (Pareto principle observed)
- Customer behavior shows repeat purchase patterns
- Significant number of one-time buyers (churn opportunity)
- Revenue distribution is skewed (high-value customers exist)

Key Findings
- Sales fluctuate monthly indicating seasonality
- UK contributes majority of revenue
- Top products drive large portion of sales
- Repeat customers contribute significantly to revenue
- Presence of one-time customers indicates churn risk
